---
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Installation">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Installation</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Sprõut requires React 19 and Tailwind CSS 4. Install the npm package and import components, or copy their source
    into your app with the shadcn CLI.
  </p>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Package setup</h2>
    <p>Add the package to your React application. Updates arrive with each release.</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="pnpm add @tulipfarm/sprout" />
    <p>
      Import Sprõut after Tailwind in your existing stylesheet. Source registration is included: no JavaScript theme
      config or extra reset is needed.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      title="app.css"
      code={`@import "tailwindcss";
@import "@tulipfarm/sprout/styles.css";`}
    />
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="App.tsx"
      code={`import {
  Sidebar,
  SidebarProvider,
  SidebarTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/sidebar";

<SidebarProvider className="min-h-dvh">
  <Sidebar label="Main navigation">
    {/* Compose your navigation here. */}
  </Sidebar>
  <main><SidebarTrigger /></main>
</SidebarProvider>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Install through shadcn</h2>
    <p>
      Every component is also a shadcn registry item. The CLI copies its source into your app, so you own and can edit
      it. Run <code>shadcn init</code> first if your app has no <code>components.json</code>.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add https://sprout.tulipfarm.ai/r/button.json" />
    <p>
      Components land in <code>components/ui</code>, helpers and icons in <code>lib/sprout</code>. The first one also
      adds Sprout base: the <code>cn()</code> helper and the design tokens. Each item brings the Sprõut components it
      uses and the CSS it needs. Every component page has the command under Installation, plus the manual steps.
    </p>
    <p>
      To type shorter names, add the registry to <code>components.json</code>:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="json"
      title="components.json"
      code={`{
  "registries": {
    "@sprout": "https://sprout.tulipfarm.ai/r/{name}.json"
  }
}`}
    />
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add @sprout/button @sprout/dialog @sprout/theme-tulipfarm" />
    <p>
      Themes install as <code>theme-&lt;name&gt;</code>, for example <code>theme-ocean</code>. The full list is in the{' '}
      <a href="/r/registry.json">registry index</a>. If your app already has a shadcn <code>button.tsx</code> or another
      file with the same name, the CLI asks before it overwrites it.
    </p>
    <p>
      To use the npm package through shadcn instead, add <code>https://sprout.tulipfarm.ai/r/sprout.json</code>. It
      installs <code>@tulipfarm/sprout</code> and adds the CSS import, and copies no source.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Existing shadcn applications</h2>
    <p>
      Keep your existing imports and theme. Sprõut uses its own <code>--sprout-*</code> variables and semantic
      utilities. No shared <code>--primary</code> or <code>--background</code> variables are replaced.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tailwind utility prefixes are not supported in this preview. Sprõut and shadcn do not promise identical props. Use
      aliases if both libraries export a component with the same name.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
